Z||000016||JohnF||12-14-2001||01:52 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackStang95:<BR><B>About 93 cents here.  You guys do realize premium gas gives you no performance benefits and may hurt it right?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>If it says 87 in your manual, 87 should go in.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Stang, I hear what you are saying.  Regardless of what the owner's manual says about octane, old engines like mine (124K+) ping under acceleration with regular.  Not with premium.  So, I DO get a benefit from the higher octane - no blown piston tops!<P>As I stated, in my SUV, regular runs great.  So that's what it gets.  <P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1578096&a=12001107&p=57211671&Sequence=0"> <BR>You can have all the SPEED you can afford!||||reg||12
Z||000017||MinnGreenGT||12-14-2001||01:59 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by PK:<BR><B>I pay £0.81/LITRE, which is £3.68($5.16) per UK gallon!!!!!!!!  <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>PK- I was over in Scotland last September- right after the "fuel crisis" ended (literally 2 days later)! And I paid out the dough to fill our rental car (Vauxhall Omega) enough to drive us almost all the way around Scotland!  I Feel your pain!<BR>-------------------------------------------<P>As to BS95's Comment about premium... if you have a high-compression engine (mine is higher than stock, but not that much higher...) you need to run premium or it will ping.  I usually run mid-grade in my GT unless I'm on a long roadtrip (I do get better mileage) and regular in my SUV winter driver.||||reg||1
Z||000018||shark93726||12-14-2001||02:07 PM||||91.9 for regular here.<P>And still going down.<P>------------------<BR>Gerald Storvik (8shark.com)||||reg||1
Z||000019||mrfiero||12-14-2001||02:08 PM||||I'm not sure if it has gone down any further, but when I filled up last week it was .959/gal for regular.   It definitely felt good to fill the tank with a ten dollar bill!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>These low prices are a direct result from the September incidents since the demand for gas has gone down (mainly due to a decrease in airline travel).  <P>Now the question is.....how many of you guys were the paranoid fools waiting in line for hours on September 11th because gas supplies were going to shrink and we were going to be paying $5/gal.?  Be honest now!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>OPEC has been trying to cut production of oil to keep the prices up, but they have had no luck so far.  Other oil producing areas haven't cut production.......Russia is the big one I am thinking of right now.  They are still in full swing trying to get on the good side of the western nations so they can be accepted into NATO (at least this is what I have heard).<P>For the time being though, we should enjoy it while we have it.......you know we will probably be back up to $1.50 or more a gallon by Memorial Day! ||||reg||10
Z||000020||FieroLisa||12-14-2001||02:25 PM||||It's about $0.88 on my side of Greensboro, NC||||reg||1
Z||000021||fieroX||12-14-2001||02:41 PM||||Were sitting around $1.03 right now.  2 weeks ago it was at $.93 but It jumped over night to 1.09, then back down.  It happened the night opec made russia cut production.  I do like the fact that russia has a vastly developing oil industry.  Give opec a run for their money. Whats funny is gas prices fluctuate so much when opec starts making threats, but we dont even get our oil from opec.  95% of our oil that isnt domestic either comes from mexico or russia.  They say russia has more oil under it than all of the middle east ever though of having.  Should allow for lower prices for some time.<P>------------------<BR>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroX.com" TARGET=_blank>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fierox.com/logo2small.gif">  </A><BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroX.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroX.com</A><BR>coming soon L67 powered 87 coupe||||reg||1
