Z||000025||JohnF||12-14-2001||04:39 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackStang95:<BR><B>...the widespread belief higher octane=higher performance.   </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You're right!  Another urban legend has been exposed.<P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1578096&a=12001107&p=57211671&Sequence=0"> <BR>You can have all the SPEED you can afford!||||reg||12
Z||000026||fieroX||12-14-2001||05:15 PM||||Older engines, say early 70's late 60's had very high compression and higher octane fuel is needed because it burns slower, and has detonation tolerance.  Any engine with 8.5:1 compression or less has no need for more than 87 octane fuel, unless you have a turbo or SC.  ||||reg||1
Z||000027||JohnF||12-14-2001||06:40 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fieroX:<BR><B>Any engine with 8.5:1 compression or less has no need for more than 87 octane fuel, unless you have a turbo or SC.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>While I certainly did not start this thread in an attempt to get everyone started AGAIN on the higher octane/compression ratios/better mileage/faster burn/just feels better/etc trip, I think it worthy to add to this response: <P>The engine sees "effective" compression ratio, not "designed" compression ratio.  While many engines were originally designed with 8.5:1 compression ratios, over the years carbon buildups have effectively raised those ratios to where is it very conceivable that a higher octane rating is required to prevent detonation (violent pre-explosions due to compression rather than a controlled burn spark (or, initially, pinging under load)) and the resultant catastrophic engine failures ranging from ring blow-by to piston blow up!<P>So, if your engine has ignition ping under any condition, up the octane 'til it quits or reduce the compression ratio (effective or designed).<P>Now, having said all that, back to "what do you pay for gas"?<P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1578096&a=12001107&p=57211671&Sequence=0"> <BR>You can have all the SPEED you can afford!||||reg||10
