Z||000040||fieroX||12-15-2001||03:56 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JohnF:<BR><B> <P>....over the years carbon buildups have effectively raised those ratios to where is it very conceivable that a higher octane rating is required to prevent detonation.....<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>actually carbon buildup doesnt raise the compression ratio (more than maybe .05), it causes hot spots in the combustion chamber, which in turn causes detonation.<P>||||reg||1
