Z||000044||JohnF||12-15-2001||07:28 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BtotheB:<BR><B>It doesn't really make a difference, just a dumb conversion... but isn't $1 CDN = $0.64 US?  (around there...)  The US dollar is worth more than the Canadian dollar... <P>45.1 in Winnipeg, eh?  Think I could drive up there and get gas, then drive back and it'd be cheaper than just getting gas here... heh</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I've only been buying gas in Canada about 6 years, but isn't $0.451/L ($1.804/3.8L) about $1.05/gal U.S.?<P>I am still paying $0.789/gal after 3 days of this thread!<P>||||reg||1
